# Production topology (issue #626).
#
# Committed with placeholders on purpose: hostnames and the preview allowlist
# are deployment facts, not repository facts, and the values that reach a
# cluster must come from the operator's own file. The deploy script copies this
# tree and overwrites this file from NCHAT_PROD_TOPOLOGY_FILE;
# validate_rendered_placeholders then refuses to apply anything still carrying
# a REPLACE_ME_* token, so an unset topology fails before kubectl, not after.
#
# CI renders the committed placeholders as-is to check the manifests' shape.
NCHAT_PROD_HOST=REPLACE_ME_PROD_HOST
NCHAT_PROD_PUBLIC_URL=REPLACE_ME_PROD_PUBLIC_URL
NCHAT_PROD_PREVIEW_ALLOW_CIDR=REPLACE_ME_PROD_PREVIEW_ALLOW_CIDR
# The browser connect-src allowlist for the shared LiveKit deployment, as the
# complete space-separated value (wss:// and https:// for the same host). Kept
# whole rather than assembled from a hostname so the CSP that reaches the
# browser is the string an operator reviewed, and so no scheme is bolted on by
# a template. It must name the production LiveKit, never a development one.
NCHAT_PROD_LIVEKIT_CONNECT_SRC=REPLACE_ME_PROD_LIVEKIT_CONNECT_SRC
